When starting NetHack on Windows 7 in any display mode (regardless of
ASCII, IBM- or DECgraphics), wrong ASCII characters are shown: 
https://sourceforge.net/apps/trac/unnethack/attachment/ticket/121/vanilla_screwed.png

Both the TTY version and the mswin GUI client from nethack.org are
affected which suggests that it is a bug in initializing the ASCII
character list or something that both versions have in common.

Workaround is to enable and disable IBM- or DECgraphics. Or if you
want to have IBMgraphics, disable IBMgraphics in defaults.nh and
enable it by hand via 'O' after startup.

Anybody an idea what's the problem here?

